   "note": "CORRECTED 2026-08 by the tantalum audit; was '+5V dig, 5.2 V, inferred, | A19, fused F5 3.15A'. Both halves of that were wrong. Traced on Figure 7-21 sheet 2 of 2 (Ch7 PDF page 81), in the POWER UP AND RESET CIRCUITRY block: C55 is not a decoupler at all, it is the CT timing capacitor of U60, a 7705A supervisor. Its top plate is the CT node -- U60 pin 3, with R52 (1 kOhm 1 %) and the RESET SWITCH SW51 on it -- and its bottom plate is GND2. The sheet annotates the block TIME CONSTANT IS 130 mSEC. In service the CT node ramps well below the rail, so 5.1 V is recorded as the hard upper bound the +5V rail sets, not as an operating value. 51 % of a 10 V part at that bound and less in practice. What matters for this one is capacitance rather than voltage: a dried-out C55 shortens or loses the power-on reset pulse."
